From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] preserve HTTP proxy authentication retries

A proxy can finish a 407 response by closing the connection without a
Content-Length header. The socket error queues a receive call, and the
subsequent disconnect also receives synchronously. Once the first call
completes the challenge and schedules authentication, the queued call sees
an empty closed socket and reports an unexpected EOF. Non-idempotent
requests then fail before their authenticated retry can start.

Ignore the stale read only while a completed reply awaits its scheduled
retry. Keep the unexpected-EOF policy for non-idempotent requests intact.
The next send clears the reply state before processing its response.

Add a local proxy regression test covering close-delimited challenges,
framing controls, rejected credentials, and incomplete responses before
and after authentication. Assert request counts and upload contents so
successful authentication cannot hide an unintended POST replay.

Origin: desktop-app; based on Qt 6.11.2.
The interacting upstream changes are:
949bebaec69d908ca842e8ef7d3e3800d8c2f7b5 (disconnect handling)
4c9a4ecd358da3bf371a2441cccd8a66c86f2d3c (non-idempotent replay protection)
Reference: https://github.com/telegramdesktop/tdesktop/issues/31474

